The signature of `route` was changed from taking `[f32; AHL_NUM_CHANNELS]` to `&[f32]`. This is a breaking change for existing users of `AhlRouter` who pass arrays directly (e.g., `router.route([1.0, 0.0, 0.0])`).

By changing the signature to accept any type that implements `AsRef<[f32]>`, we can support both arrays and slices seamlessly, preserving 100% backward compatibility.

