![critical](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/critical.svg)

If `ChannelRouter` is deserialized from an older version (or using default values), `channel_fatigue` and `baseline_weights` will be empty vectors. Accessing `self.channel_fatigue[i]` or `self.baseline_weights[i]` will then cause a runtime panic due to out-of-bounds indexing. We should lazily initialize/resize these vectors to `n` if their lengths do not match.

```rust
        // Ensure neuromodulatory state vectors are properly sized (e.g. after deserialization)
        if self.channel_fatigue.len() != n {
            self.channel_fatigue.resize(n, 0.0);
        }
        if self.baseline_weights.len() != n {
            self.baseline_weights = self.neurons.iter().map(|neu| neu.weights.clone()).collect();
        }

        // Compute effective thresholds per channel.
        let mut effective_thresholds = vec![0.0f32; n];
        let mut effective_leaks = vec![0.0f32; n];
```

